-- title:
--   Flat surjective pullback is injective on ideal sheaves
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes (in a fixed universe) and let $\pi \colon Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes that is flat and surjective. The assertion is that the function sending a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on $X$ to its inverse image along $\pi$ is injective. Here ideal sheaves are taken in the form `X.IdealSheafData`, i.e. the datum of an ideal of $\Gamma(X, U)$ for every affine open $U \subseteq X$, subject to the compatibility condition that for affine opens $V \subseteq U$ the ideal attached to $V$ is obtained from the one attached to $U$ by base change along the localisation map; and `I.comap π` is the corresponding inverse image ideal sheaf datum on $Y$, whose ideal on an affine open $V$ of $Y$ is generated by the pullbacks of the sections of $I$. Thus for quasi-coherent ideals $I, J \subseteq \mathcal{O}_X$, the equality $I \cdot \mathcal{O}_Y = J \cdot \mathcal{O}_Y$ forces $I = J$. No quasi-compactness or finiteness hypothesis on $\pi$, $X$ or $Y$ is imposed, and both flatness and surjectivity are hypotheses of the statement.
--
--   This is the descent statement that a faithfully flat (here: flat and surjective) morphism of schemes detects quasi-coherent ideals, the global form of the fact that extension of ideals along a faithfully flat ring map is injective. It is used in the treatment of relative effective Cartier divisors, where it gives uniqueness of a divisor with prescribed pullback: it is cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelEffCartierDiv.pullbackAlong_injective`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelEffCartierDiv.pullbackAlong_injective) and by [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelEffCartierDiv.existsUnique_pullbackAlong_eq_of_isPullback_of_isAffine`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelEffCartierDiv.existsUnique_pullbackAlong_eq_of_isPullback_of_isAffine).
